Aibell.Archive.Rar is a C# implementation of the RAR 3.x/4.x and RAR 5.0 decompressors written, in its own structure, from the
BSD-licensed RAR readers of libarchive (archive_read_support_format_rar.c and archive_read_support_format_rar5.c, https://libarchive.org)
and the public-domain PPMd variant H code (Dmitry Shkarin, 2001; Igor Pavlov, 2010) that libarchive bundles as archive_ppmd7.c.
RAR is a trademark of Alexander Roshal; this project contains no code from RARLAB's UnRAR and does not create RAR archives.

